--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-2 After Battle Cutscene
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I had nine sisters and a brother. Our father was a model parent. He
      gave us the education that was suitable in a family that was neither rich nor
      poor. He was creative and careful with saving money, which allowed him to build
      two houses. One of the two became the house that I lived in with a nipa hut
      nearby, shaded with banana trees, where I had fond memories of.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "At night I prayed along with my mother and siblings. Afterwards, we
      went to the roof to enjoy the moonlight; and our nurse would tell us stories.
      Sometimes sad, sometimes happy, the nurse\u2019s stories were unique in their
      imagination. In these stories, dead people, gold, and plants on which diamonds
      grew were all mixed together."
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: When I was four years of age, my little sister Concha died, and for
      the first time I cried because of love and regret. Until then I had shed tears
      only for my own mistakes, which my loving, wise mother knew how to correct.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 6
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I learned to write in my own village. My father looked after my education.
      He paid an old man, who had been his schoolmate, to teach me the first steps
      in Latin. This teacher lived in our house till he died, five months later.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: In June of 1868, I went to Manila with my father. We went and rode
      a boat, and I cannot tell how happy I was at each new stop on the banks of
      the Pasig. A few years later, we went to Cainta, Taytay, and Antipolo, and
      then to Manila. In Santa Ana I visited my eldest sister, Saturnina, who at
      that time was a student in La Concordia College. Then I returned to my village
      and remained until 1870.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 4
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "Now it's time to go to Bi\xF1an."
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: And with Chapter 1 finished, now we go to the next Chapter.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: 
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "Chapter II: My Schooling and Daily Life in Bi\xF1an"
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
